Chris,

Thanks. The key thing was the single NA in the non-working data frame (I got confused and thought "all known" meant "no NAs" in your original post). In the current CRAN version there can't  be any NAs in the newdata.

This is partially fixed in this update <https://github.com/rbchan/unmarked/commit/f3db5487f5607551f6344fc7813a52b2f60eee1f> to the Github version of unmarked, which should at least allow prediction when se.fit=F. I discovered another bug in the process of looking at your issue that causes problems when se.fit=T, but it should be an easy fix. I'll send another PR to Richard, who is surely getting tired of all my little bugfixes!

Thanks for helping me sort out these issues.

Ken

